    "title": "Two People “Speak on Condition of Anonymity” About Why Sean Penn Skipped the 2026 Oscars",
    "text": "One Battle After Another – official trailer (Warner Bros.)Digital Spy GBLIVECurrent Time 0:00Total Duration 2:24Sean Penn just won the Oscar for Best Actor at the 2026 Academy Awards but...didn’t show up to collect his award. Instead, Kieran Culkin accepted the statue on his behalf, saying, “Sean Penn couldn’t be here this evening or didn’t want to. So I’ll be accepting this award on his behalf.”This content is imported from x. You may be able to find the same content in another format, or you may be able to find more information, at their web site.So...where was Sean? Unclear, but he also skipped the Actor Awards and the BAFTAs this year. The New York Times reports that Sean “headed to Europe” and that “his plan as of late last week was to visit Ukraine, according to two people who spoke on the condition of anonymity because they were not authorized to discuss the matter.”These people “did not specify what he would be doing there or where precisely within the country he would be going” and there’s a “possibility” that his “itinerary might have changed.” Meanwhile, his rep declined to comment to the outlet!Other nominees in Sean’s category were Stellan Skarsgard for Sentimental Value, Jacob Elordi for Frankenstein, Delroy Lindo for Sinners, and Benicio Del Toro for One Battle After Another.",
